<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <section id="privacy-page" class="py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <span class="rounded-full border border-warning/25 bg-warning/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-warning-foreground">
          Draft—legal review required
        </span>
        <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Private-alpha draft · 16 September 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-6xl">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        This plain-language draft describes the public design-partner application and the invite-only monitoring workspace. It must be reviewed and replaced or approved by qualified counsel before broader external use.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 border-t border-border pt-10 text-base leading-7">
        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collect">
          <h2 id="privacy-collect" class="text-xl font-semibold">Information collected</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            The design-partner application collects your name, work email, company, role, a description of the LLM workflow you want to monitor, the problem you face today, whether you use OpenAI, Anthropic, or both, and whether you can participate in recurring feedback. If invited, the workspace stores your account and membership, encrypted provider credential, prompt and frozen test context, test inputs, provider outputs, deterministic contract, baseline, evaluation evidence, alerts, and review decisions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-use">
          <h2 id="privacy-use" class="text-xl font-semibold">How it is used</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            Application information is used to evaluate product fit, contact applicants, and learn which deterministic monitoring requirements recur. Workspace data is used to execute the test requests you authorize, compare them with a compatible historical baseline, explain alerts, and preserve reproducible review history. Strict product-learning events contain bounded stages, categories, IDs, counts, and statuses rather than prompts, outputs, credentials, emails, or free-form notes. Submitting the public form does not create an account or subscription.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-not-collected">
          <h2 id="privacy-not-collected" class="text-xl font-semibold">
            What the public form does not collect
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            Do not submit provider credentials, production prompts, model outputs, personal customer data, confidential documents, or regulated information through the application form. The form does not request payment information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-retention">
          <h2 id="privacy-retention" class="text-xl font-semibold">Retention and requests</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            Raw workspace evidence is retained while the workspace is active. Closing a workspace immediately stops execution, revokes provider credentials, and starts a 30-day recovery window. An explicit deletion request stops execution and is scheduled for irreversible deletion within seven days. Encrypted disaster-recovery backups expire within 30 days; a content-free deletion receipt remains after purge. Applicants and invited users should use the verified communication channel through which they received access for privacy requests.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes">
          <h2 id="privacy-changes" class="text-xl font-semibold">Changes to this draft</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            This notice will change as the alpha evolves. Material changes to account access, monitored data, operational providers, retention, or deletion must be reflected here and reviewed before broader release.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.app>
